<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Glarentza</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Clarentza, Clarence</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Glarentza was a medieval port on the north-western coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a>, near modern Kyllini, and the main harbour of the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a>, where its mint struck coins. It passed to Constantine Palaiologos in 1428 and was later largely abandoned.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/glarentza.jpg" alt="Glarentza" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chris06 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2022_Church_of_St_Francis_ruin,_Glarentza_(01).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
